-- title:
--   The image of prime multiplication is Zariski constructible
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a commutative algebraic group over a Philippon base field $K$, and let $p$ be a prime integer. In the Zariski topology on the actual group points, the image of multiplication by $p$ is constructible:
--   $$[p]G(K)=\{p x:x\in G(K)\}\quad\text{is constructible in }G(K).$$
--   Thus the image belongs to the Boolean algebra generated by Zariski-open subsets. This is the constructibility input for converting a local dominance statement into a nonempty open set of divisible points. Connectedness is not assumed, and zero-dimensional groups are included.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The statement uses the repository's concrete product of locally closed projective embeddings and its induced polynomial Zariski topology. It is an auxiliary application of Chevalley's theorem and the comparison with closed points over an algebraically closed field. The construction of the multiplication morphism and comparison of its image with the concrete point set remain Open.
-- source:
--   Stacks Project, Theorem 10.29.10 (Chevalley), tag 00FE, https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FE ; Lemma 10.35.22, tag 00GE, https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00GE . Auxiliary application to multiplication on finite-type algebraic groups, using affine charts and closed-point comparison over an algebraically closed field. The concrete embedded-group/morphism bridge remains Open.

import Mathlib.Topology.Constructible
import Definitions.Def_PhilipponMultiplicity_Geometry
set_option autoImplicit false

namespace PhilipponMultiplicity

theorem prime_nsmul_range_is_constructible
    (K : Type*) [NontriviallyNormedField K] (hK : IsPhilipponBaseField K)
    (G : EmbeddedGroupProduct K) (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) :
    @Topology.IsConstructible G.Point G.zariskiTopology (Set.range (fun x : G.Point => p • x)) := by sorry

end PhilipponMultiplicity
